# Coin Change - Minimum Coins Solution (Obfuscated Recursive Implementation)

## Main Goal
This code solves the classic **"Minimum Coin Change" problem**: given a set of coin denominations and a target amount, it calculates the **minimum number of coins needed to make up that amount**, using a recursive brute-force approach.

## How It Works

The code has been obfuscated (likely through decompilation, as noted in the comment), replacing standard operators with small helper methods and inserting dead code (`"".length()`, `null == null` check) that has no functional effect but disguises the logic. Stripped down, the logic is:

```java
public static int minCoins(int[] coins, int n, int amount) {
    if (amount == 0) return 0;
    int result = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        if (coins[i] <= amount) {
            int sub = minCoins(coins, n, amount - coins[i]);
            if (sub != Integer.MAX_VALUE && sub + 1 < result) {
                result = sub + 1;
            }
        }
    }
    return result;
}
```

