# Abundant Number Checker Analysis

## Main Goal
This code determines whether a given integer `n` is an **abundant number** — a number whose proper divisors (divisors excluding the number itself) sum to a value greater than the number itself.

## How It Works

The code has been obfuscated (likely via decompilation) with meaningless method names and dead/junk code injected to obscure control flow. Stripped of the obfuscation, the logic is equivalent to:

```java
public static boolean isAbundant(int n) {
    int sum = 0;
    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
        if (n % i == 0) {
            sum += i;
        }
    }
    return sum > n;
}
```

